user_prompt:
You are evaluating ONE news article against ONE forecast scenario.

The scenario was published on {forecast_generated_at} as part of a Three Horizons forecast for the topic "{topic}". The article was published AFTER the forecast.

--- SCENARIO BEING EVALUATED ---
Horizon: {scenario_type}
Title: {scenario_title}
Description: {scenario_description}
Timeframe: {scenario_timeframe}
Sentiment (forecast's expected direction): {scenario_sentiment}

--- SIBLING SCENARIOS (the other scenarios in the same forecast — only use these to decide "better_fits_other_scenario") ---
{sibling_scenarios_digest}

--- ARTICLE ---
Title: {article_title}
Date: {article_date}
Summary: {article_summary}

--- DECISION RULES ---
Return exactly one verdict from this list:

- "supports_trajectory": The article reports concrete evidence (an event, decision, study, milestone, or measurable trend) consistent with the direction the scenario predicts. Not just "related topic."
- "supports_state_contradicts_trajectory": The article confirms the SUBJECT of the scenario but suggests the trajectory is stabilising, reversing, or being mitigated.
- "contradicts": The article reports evidence that runs against the scenario's predicted direction.
- "better_fits_other_scenario": The article is on-topic but more clearly fits a SIBLING scenario than this one. Provide best_alt_scenario_idx.
- "neutral_context": Generic background or commentary about the topic, no directional evidence.
- "unrelated": Article is off-topic for this scenario.

Also classify the EVIDENCE TYPE:
- "milestone": A specific, dated, named event the scenario foreshadowed (a policy passed, a study published, a product launched, an entity collapsed).
- "leading_indicator": An early empirical signal the scenario expected (a statistic moving in the predicted direction, a new entrant, a budget shift).
- "commentary": Opinion, op-ed, analysis discussing the trend without new evidence.
- "anecdote": A single example or case study, suggestive but not generalisable.

--- OUTPUT ---
Return ONLY this JSON object, no other text:
{
  "verdict": "<one of the six values above>",
  "best_alt_scenario_idx": <int or null>,
  "evidence_type": "<milestone|leading_indicator|commentary|anecdote>",
  "confidence": <0.0-1.0>,
  "rationale": "<one sentence, max 30 words, citing the specific fact from the article that drove the verdict>"
}
